  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile with avgpool, especially scvi_n200, which reached 0.650 accuracy and 0.628 F1, clearly above PCA multiprofile avgpool at 0.591/0.573. Aggregation also appears important, since avgpool beat transformer for PCA. The main remaining uncertainty is whether another learned RNA representation, scgpt, can match or exceed scvi under the same favorable profile and aggregation settings. config_008 changes only the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while keeping multiprofile and avgpool, so it isolates the representation effect. This is the best next use of budget because it exploits the current best profile/aggregation setting, tests an unexplored important design choice, and avoids premature multimodal fusion before the best unimodal representation is established."
}

